1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,668
Angstrom Signals has two price charts.

2
00:00:02,718 --> 00:00:06,602
The fast chart, built for trading, and the classic chart, the original.

3
00:00:06,652 --> 00:00:09,363
Both use the same readings and indicators.

4
00:00:09,800 --> 00:00:12,319
Pick one in Settings, under Price chart.

5
00:00:12,369 --> 00:00:16,530
TradingView is the fast chart, and it's the one we'll use in this series.

6
00:00:18,066 --> 00:00:22,825
Click any asset in the signal tables, and it opens in the Interactive Chart.

7
00:00:23,277 --> 00:00:26,248
Choose the candle size, from five minutes to monthly,

8
00:00:26,268 --> 00:00:28,825
and how much history the chart opens on.

9
00:00:28,875 --> 00:00:32,140
A crossed-out range doesn't work with that candle size.

10
00:00:39,992 --> 00:00:43,471
Scroll to zoom in and out, and drag to move back in time.

11
00:00:43,521 --> 00:00:46,378
The two buttons at the top right go back to your range,

12
00:00:46,398 --> 00:00:48,215
or jump to the newest candle.

13
00:00:48,677 --> 00:00:50,321
Point at any candle.

14
00:00:50,371 --> 00:00:53,588
The legend at the top shows its open, high, low and close,

15
00:00:53,608 --> 00:00:56,196
and the value of every line on the chart.

16
00:00:56,673 --> 00:00:59,469
Turn indicators on and off with these pills.

17
00:00:59,519 --> 00:01:03,062
Panels such as Stoch RSI open underneath the price.

18
00:01:03,112 --> 00:01:06,249
All and Clear, at the end of the row, switch them all at once.

19
00:01:10,752 --> 00:01:13,932
Drag the bar under the chart to make it taller or shorter.

20
00:01:13,982 --> 00:01:16,330
Your choices are saved to your account.

21
00:01:16,767 --> 00:01:18,347
That's the basics.

22
00:01:18,397 --> 00:01:18,648
Next:

23
00:01:18,668 --> 00:01:23,094
the drawing tools, the price levels traders watch, the signals drawn on the chart,

24
00:01:23,114 --> 00:01:24,606
and planning an entry.
